-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Beta testing grant
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This section applies only to pre-release versions, meaning any version numbered
below 1.0.0. It exists so that people can help test the software before it is
finished.

You are permitted, free of charge, to:

  1. Download and install unmodified copies of a pre-release version.
  2. Run it on Minecraft servers that you own or operate, including servers that
     take donations or sell ranks.
  3. Modify your own copy locally for the purpose of diagnosing a problem, and
     share those changes with the copyright holder as a bug report.

You are not permitted to:

  1. Redistribute the software, modified or not, to anyone else. Point people at
     the official source instead.
  2. Publish it on any plugin marketplace, mirror, or download site.
  3. Sell it, or bundle it into anything sold, including server packs.
  4. Remove or alter this notice.

This grant is revocable at any time and for any reason, and it ends
automatically when version 1.0.0 is released. Revocation means you stop using
it; it does not require you to do anything else.

Reports, logs, and suggestions you send about the software may be used to
improve it, without obligation or compensation. Nothing here transfers ownership
of your server data, worlds, or configuration - the software sends nothing
anywhere unless you configure a Discord webhook yourself.

Testing software is testing software. It has bugs, it has been wrong before, and
it may be wrong on your server. Run it with `remediation.auto-apply` left off,
on a server you can afford to have misbehave. The warranty disclaimer below
applies in full, and applies especially here.


